 "findings": {
  "_note": "Run-specific FINDINGS. They live with the data, never in the generator — hardcoding them would make the tool's reusability claim false.",
  "fire": "The chain COMPLETES. 19 statewide credentials, 90.2 deduplicated units across 35 distinct receiving courses, several C-ID-carrying. Those courses are really taught (64 / 56 / 40 colleges). 38 of 63 colleges with a Fire program have adopted no fire CPL.",
  "wildland": "The chain HALF-COMPLETES. 6 statewide credentials, 15.0 units, 5 receiving courses named 'Wildland 101-105 (Wildland Fire Behavior)' — which NO college teaches under that name, though 58 colleges teach 293 wildland courses. 16 of 19 colleges with a Wildland program have adopted nothing.",
  "electrical": "The chain BREAKS at the course step. 12 statewide credentials (IBEW, NCCER 1-4, C-10, C-46, both apprenticeships) collapse onto 4 generic construction courses worth 11.5-18 units with NO C-IDs. Rough Electrical is taught at 1 college, Construction Law at 4 — against 1,047 electrical-trade courses at 106 colleges. 53 of 63 colleges with an Electrical program have adopted nothing.",
  "caljac": "Cal-JAC has exactly 5 credentials in MAP, identified by issuer. Four are statewide; the fifth — Firefighter Journeyperson Certificate, the apprenticeship completion — is flagged LOCAL yet carries the highest potential-adopter count of the five (98). The ladder is missing its bottom rung.",
  "wffs_absent": "Wildland Fire Fighter Specialist, named explicitly in the request, appears NOWHERE in MAP — zero hits across all 2,903 exhibit records, searching unified titles AND the raw college-entered titles. Build-new, first-in-state.",
  "dedup": "Summing credential unit values overstates what a student can bank: fire sums naively to 147.2u but the distinct receiving-course ceiling is 90.2u (39% double-counted), because Firefighter 1, Firefighter EMT Certificate and the Fire Officer series all name the same courses.",
  "exemplars": "City College of San Francisco is the wildland exemplar (all 6 statewide wildland credentials, the only college with the full set). Cabrillo College is the electrical exemplar (all 12, 86.5u). San Diego Miramar leads fire at 132.0u."
